[{:db/id "q-124234/selection/a9643e1e9d640a516d6d616ca64d520542c12081a3672d25c1562d82453d139e" :answer/id #uuid "137e285f-f438-5ac7-a77d-89cf5ba6dec2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}+4t+2)\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124234/selection/9c09ded43168b71189721b4ddd5f3e530e9c01901cdc2efe45157f2ae4fafea3" :answer/id #uuid "e6cfc9ca-d0a8-5a0b-876a-1220296b047f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}+5t)\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124234/selection/a4a25403c71edb13b46b52f7096e31fe6badd330c6982e174580a2fd96946ec6" :answer/id #uuid "71764e77-ad9c-53d0-b928-9e19ee3d1cce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}+5t)\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124234/selection/6718426bee99b559ecaa16ce6aa4e58bfa71512839de279569c225f9875b2c14" :answer/id #uuid "10050710-a6c6-5ceb-a235-fac3b3effa01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}+5t+2)\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124234/selection/6e4f167664c61c46aeb6d0b01aa431b6811af1c780ee453424a9e9d34ad199d0" :answer/id #uuid "1fb507fb-68cf-59d6-b62e-76fca8ccfc0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}+4t+2)\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124234/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c00241e5-6453-5258-8de5-525767c76a89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124234/selection/9c09ded43168b71189721b4ddd5f3e530e9c01901cdc2efe45157f2ae4fafea3" :answer-field/choices ["q-124234/selection/a9643e1e9d640a516d6d616ca64d520542c12081a3672d25c1562d82453d139e" "q-124234/selection/9c09ded43168b71189721b4ddd5f3e530e9c01901cdc2efe45157f2ae4fafea3" "q-124234/selection/a4a25403c71edb13b46b52f7096e31fe6badd330c6982e174580a2fd96946ec6" "q-124234/selection/6718426bee99b559ecaa16ce6aa4e58bfa71512839de279569c225f9875b2c14" "q-124234/selection/6e4f167664c61c46aeb6d0b01aa431b6811af1c780ee453424a9e9d34ad199d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124234" :question/id #uuid "2477d9bd-885a-5f6e-90f9-b849c79e63e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-124234" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/43c8d1ced440e0fe79052c1329ff3af865e1fdbfb4cc0c7ad0a9c176592358e9.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment from the point $(-1,1)$ to the point $(2,2),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨3t-1,\\,t+1⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(-1,1)$ and $(2,2).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(-1+t(2-(-1))),\\,(1+t(2-1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3t-1,\\,t+1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-1)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x+{y}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(3t-1)+(t+1)^{2} \\\\  & =(3t-1)+({t}^{2}+2t+1) \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+5t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}+5t)\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}+5t)\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124234/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c243e957-272a-5bde-8878-7264a94e447e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124234"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124221/selection/cc550a2c452bccc5558ee40486222086ea318d2a8a27654ca720132f7aa5bd70" :answer/id #uuid "9796bc7f-7fd5-5a1b-96a0-0fa43a5757d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124221/selection/e192e210ea9a46fd94a9f8ffe9a7c621f93835451f5a405116f91d303310ef87" :answer/id #uuid "2db8e5de-2b53-5ac5-ac26-602ca82b070c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-16{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124221/selection/8bbc0b7a107b5e0e66881e386f25703f8b458bbbc900c3dda8223c1be638b46d" :answer/id #uuid "96e18587-bf1f-56af-8197-fab0d5bdc60d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124221/selection/aa3e372ed36b0f38b0bcaaebe474bb4d002fc6d8eaeb865dbcc41b7b747db4dc" :answer/id #uuid "910846b1-fc47-501c-9c9c-62423acd0300" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124221/selection/740b416b35e9d7df7e93123e37d783bdb893646b56340dbbc5f0a56f505caa75" :answer/id #uuid "770fd2b6-1229-5827-85a0-bd9bd9042941" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124221/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "24bf9397-014b-54c3-8049-916703a1ec5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124221/selection/e192e210ea9a46fd94a9f8ffe9a7c621f93835451f5a405116f91d303310ef87" :answer-field/choices ["q-124221/selection/cc550a2c452bccc5558ee40486222086ea318d2a8a27654ca720132f7aa5bd70" "q-124221/selection/e192e210ea9a46fd94a9f8ffe9a7c621f93835451f5a405116f91d303310ef87" "q-124221/selection/8bbc0b7a107b5e0e66881e386f25703f8b458bbbc900c3dda8223c1be638b46d" "q-124221/selection/aa3e372ed36b0f38b0bcaaebe474bb4d002fc6d8eaeb865dbcc41b7b747db4dc" "q-124221/selection/740b416b35e9d7df7e93123e37d783bdb893646b56340dbbc5f0a56f505caa75"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124221" :question/id #uuid "6572425b-1f69-589f-ade1-f4702feda38e" :question/math-academy-id "q-124221" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/9babf4c2ec631b3b872760261a46c3552cb93b93df90515ff0605c15043841ca.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along a circle of radius $4,$ traversed from the point $(-4,0)$ to the point $(4,0),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $4$ centered at $O.$ It can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\pi \\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x+y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-16{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124221/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c243e957-272a-5bde-8878-7264a94e447e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124221"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-124230"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/1b693165c8f6201e96f0a972746324c65a308d1f143f229c465b6aa22b7aeb16.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}(x-y)\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along the ellipse $16{x}^{2}+25{y}^{2}=400,$ traversed from the point $(0,-4)$ to the point $(5,0),$ as shown above?\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x-y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)(-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-5{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-124218/selection/cf560750198a5b909d033c3fa72d9e3be9f4b026ef6c9707f8793f1e06781925" :answer/id #uuid "d048c409-7c97-5ec3-9915-2a8d53c6d5f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124218/selection/ca6580d8c8b2c5a8d230c71af2794a7f6c8e136116b2a7b77915591385d76b95" :answer/id #uuid "b459da0f-9fa9-5c17-85e4-fae984d3b326" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124218/selection/68d12ab82b0782936c0e8845803ae3f8f5c93b5cb0054c5e85f95c1a82f99497" :answer/id #uuid "bb258125-adcc-5ed3-b42a-066ec0ab384f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124218/selection/2b5f54fcafd5f28ca50720a60cab16f26e47df4e68af9763c279953186930819" :answer/id #uuid "b9bdbb7b-903e-528e-b6ac-b88102408f62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124218/selection/24e6829aaf9bd819fdbda0b4c7d852dfc2606468db571e75a59f2462ed1dc020" :answer/id #uuid "7f433c6a-cd0b-58c0-927f-3a7f5124ab97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124218/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c4a3174-dead-59df-8e0e-20fac7a0fc06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124218/selection/2b5f54fcafd5f28ca50720a60cab16f26e47df4e68af9763c279953186930819" :answer-field/choices ["q-124218/selection/cf560750198a5b909d033c3fa72d9e3be9f4b026ef6c9707f8793f1e06781925" "q-124218/selection/ca6580d8c8b2c5a8d230c71af2794a7f6c8e136116b2a7b77915591385d76b95" "q-124218/selection/68d12ab82b0782936c0e8845803ae3f8f5c93b5cb0054c5e85f95c1a82f99497" "q-124218/selection/2b5f54fcafd5f28ca50720a60cab16f26e47df4e68af9763c279953186930819" "q-124218/selection/24e6829aaf9bd819fdbda0b4c7d852dfc2606468db571e75a59f2462ed1dc020"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124218" :question/id #uuid "76ca20f1-204f-59f9-8369-ed13b85fecd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-124218" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/4727c988042bd8d63af370c507db8988b3024cf7e75c86d40bc70cdcfd744873.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}y{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along a circle of radius $2,$ traversed from the point $(0,2)$ to the point $(-2,0),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $2$ centered at $O.$ It can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=y{e}^{x},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot {e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot {e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124218/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c243e957-272a-5bde-8878-7264a94e447e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124218"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124223/selection/cd253cca5abbf432ecac81e550cb14611ec42dbe6d0f3503ca4872427f5a6b23" :answer/id #uuid "4c660b47-d26d-5837-bf87-b4d55e6267c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124223/selection/f82b15c1aad672f6fb35debc44529c9099bf70dba979ad9291b15a39fdde3620" :answer/id #uuid "d01dd8cc-1825-5fe6-9c05-a0176642a931" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{cos}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124223/selection/13d2d4473278ffcbcef6e14d879eeb4fba0d9d01b63748a71f1b2b5c6c527839" :answer/id #uuid "9fa61b2c-1e4b-5b2c-94a5-2feda52c8a62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{sin}^{3}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124223/selection/08e7304142eb789db8aa1ab2ce280db93648f13caf90f99553e8613de6dc29d7" :answer/id #uuid "ee224196-475f-560b-9e18-6377f02c2982" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{sin}^{3}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124223/selection/a39da94bf52244a15bcdb7baf55520add3fa4bb07e636a8155c383c3ee1ed038" :answer/id #uuid "b5f1e244-bf4b-55d5-b097-f5c31b3e6ac7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124223/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4189e67f-833f-570f-a4e8-fc3cd384279f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124223/selection/13d2d4473278ffcbcef6e14d879eeb4fba0d9d01b63748a71f1b2b5c6c527839" :answer-field/choices ["q-124223/selection/cd253cca5abbf432ecac81e550cb14611ec42dbe6d0f3503ca4872427f5a6b23" "q-124223/selection/f82b15c1aad672f6fb35debc44529c9099bf70dba979ad9291b15a39fdde3620" "q-124223/selection/13d2d4473278ffcbcef6e14d879eeb4fba0d9d01b63748a71f1b2b5c6c527839" "q-124223/selection/08e7304142eb789db8aa1ab2ce280db93648f13caf90f99553e8613de6dc29d7" "q-124223/selection/a39da94bf52244a15bcdb7baf55520add3fa4bb07e636a8155c383c3ee1ed038"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124223" :question/id #uuid "433fdc74-35b8-5b39-ab17-f3d230761caa" :question/math-academy-id "q-124223" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/2f01c4633489a913d93f86ccc83580963ea5cd41bed31347108730a7d60c3ebf.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along the ellipse $3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=3,$ traversed from the point $(0,\\sqrt{3})$ to the point $(0,-\\sqrt{3}),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x{y}^{2}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{sin}^{2}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-3{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{sin}^{3}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124223/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c243e957-272a-5bde-8878-7264a94e447e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124223"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-124121"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/36b985c811eb28d8220017c6b7407b3a104554d785dafdb35f17553c262bdc35.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}xy\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment from the point $(-1,-2)$ to the point $(2,4),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨3t-1,\\,6t-2⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(-1,-2)$ and $(2,4).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(-1+t(2-(-1))),\\,(-2+t(4-(-2)))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3t-1,\\,6t-2⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6t-2)=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=xy$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(3t-1)\\cdot (6t-2) \\\\  & =18{t}^{2}-12t+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(18{t}^{2}-12t+2)\\cdot 6\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =12{\\int }_{0}^{1}(9{t}^{2}-6t+1)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-124293/selection/093e7d6921eb2d8676b8d9458fa90cebe351a930ed90f2ae591bdf6a7bcbcf97" :answer/id #uuid "29c45407-92cb-53b5-bd3d-48509f75cbb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124293/selection/ab4d997e7ac9947dd6493561aaaa975712979e6b2c7d4d99c82240f19e271f3d" :answer/id #uuid "9c6633e7-54ac-5963-bbc4-e1435478ed17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124293/selection/874cd070bcc01ad5b054ecb3eb4834d793c7e7940d80ece62131e6530db0e02e" :answer/id #uuid "a3784859-363f-50e1-a7a7-d984ed022519" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124293/selection/e0ea0cc9b32b74e03f9dd4a33c7395dba673239a6eb5bbc55ebc5375479542a7" :answer/id #uuid "02d875fd-2b57-5da8-9ba1-9d9b20c0e1bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124293/selection/4055f71771a7b2445137bccb49338e99f5b699a1eb7d9cab87728841ffb63b96" :answer/id #uuid "4f96e6b5-79f2-5a4b-bff3-d89a9f983389" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124293/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fcaf5eb1-25b9-578b-9fb7-9f324d282f6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124293/selection/874cd070bcc01ad5b054ecb3eb4834d793c7e7940d80ece62131e6530db0e02e" :answer-field/choices ["q-124293/selection/093e7d6921eb2d8676b8d9458fa90cebe351a930ed90f2ae591bdf6a7bcbcf97" "q-124293/selection/ab4d997e7ac9947dd6493561aaaa975712979e6b2c7d4d99c82240f19e271f3d" "q-124293/selection/874cd070bcc01ad5b054ecb3eb4834d793c7e7940d80ece62131e6530db0e02e" "q-124293/selection/e0ea0cc9b32b74e03f9dd4a33c7395dba673239a6eb5bbc55ebc5375479542a7" "q-124293/selection/4055f71771a7b2445137bccb49338e99f5b699a1eb7d9cab87728841ffb63b96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124293" :question/id #uuid "e84b6989-0b06-5564-bfd3-0660ddb2a037" :question/math-academy-id "q-124293" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/4d02a56e1f927ccf8bd76a6fcc46dec61259649176695912865dd050657ce7f0.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}xy\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along a quarter of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=4,$ traversed from the point $(0,1)$ to the point $(-2,0),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=xy,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124293/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0712bb6-c0f8-5551-8362-ae23629aa618"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124293"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124270/selection/97ce3bada7708d636136f813536b9a93fc6737c4ce22a42259e51cb6ab88fd86" :answer/id #uuid "faf6a9e7-fa4c-5553-9d3e-ca6d62c5784d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{t}^{2}+7t+1)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124270/selection/b2e25785a395c5340ed884b8804a00b62b62df77f9aa96a299dcbbbcddff9669" :answer/id #uuid "3835bca5-3ee8-5a5e-b4de-327c61bbbc6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{t}^{2}-t+7)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124270/selection/f0ee41baff40fc98ed0bc91d356823b939b2d4464e746ebbfb959dccf21caecd" :answer/id #uuid "54135e8b-9a76-5637-836f-2fd519fa14a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{1}(6{t}^{2}+5)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124270/selection/d37f2a09da4c3c6ee8c46aa979cf6f2a79f8e0e72938b7d17a71945a2c124ea8" :answer/id #uuid "e12d14ef-cbe6-595b-bca9-922041d36715" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}(18{t}^{2}+t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124270/selection/50fc83f3fd6401ecae8b600b98dc8d8961a5aed89580aa1310d164ad5930c9a3" :answer/id #uuid "366f2d34-c110-5f54-9dfe-34c4644dd0fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}(9{t}^{2}-8t+2)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124270/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4974625a-2b14-5828-abbd-2b99ac3389c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124270/selection/50fc83f3fd6401ecae8b600b98dc8d8961a5aed89580aa1310d164ad5930c9a3" :answer-field/choices ["q-124270/selection/97ce3bada7708d636136f813536b9a93fc6737c4ce22a42259e51cb6ab88fd86" "q-124270/selection/b2e25785a395c5340ed884b8804a00b62b62df77f9aa96a299dcbbbcddff9669" "q-124270/selection/f0ee41baff40fc98ed0bc91d356823b939b2d4464e746ebbfb959dccf21caecd" "q-124270/selection/d37f2a09da4c3c6ee8c46aa979cf6f2a79f8e0e72938b7d17a71945a2c124ea8" "q-124270/selection/50fc83f3fd6401ecae8b600b98dc8d8961a5aed89580aa1310d164ad5930c9a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124270" :question/id #uuid "5a2ef7fe-3111-5563-a01f-31b1b4cdc9b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-124270" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/58995f1bc5b45dbe0d30a9d0cbf704d792b955e7195c0e4dc3610ddf2e576579.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}({x}^{2}-y)\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment from the point $(-1,-1)$ to the point $(2,1),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨3t-1,\\,2t-1⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(-1,-1)$ and $(2,1).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(-1+t(2-(-1))),\\,(-1+t(1-(-1)))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3t-1,\\,2t-1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-1)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(3t-1)^{2}-(2t-1) \\\\  & =9{t}^{2}-6t+1-2t+1 \\\\  & =9{t}^{2}-8t+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(9{t}^{2}-8t+2)\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}(9{t}^{2}-8t+2)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124270/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0712bb6-c0f8-5551-8362-ae23629aa618"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124270"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124298/selection/a67ba2ed67a73986443abb874c97f0c95a8b36be477f216946792b35dd801315" :answer/id #uuid "cb52cbb6-cf9c-51df-993f-3786ba588cdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(3{sin}^{2}⁡t+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124298/selection/d2ce58dcfde67b9e3e33c40dc0ec67c44464d31bf77f451e3f12f8c5805836bc" :answer/id #uuid "5d143156-3dc9-5d88-883c-353d1d0a84d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }({sin}^{2}⁡t+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124298/selection/b5742563c1be9789c9972480cc0398a9d68a3b4422fef1cb034bdb05841d249f" :answer/id #uuid "bcc59397-32d6-581c-b145-5fe8c302cfee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }({sin}^{2}⁡t+3){sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124298/selection/f64772e64adfa06dcdc8b7e41d95f5a9112e5a1d7e5522bf9f6875c584882b1e" :answer/id #uuid "b70628f3-57a5-5d87-8987-7d9fa61a1513" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }({sin}^{2}⁡t+3){cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124298/selection/98deb7f86f2e63ffd173e7b088d57fe256d622326f7ab344397f6876c121375f" :answer/id #uuid "006a4d9d-2287-5a40-85ce-4062ce2e4bda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(3{sin}^{2}⁡t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124298/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5d198c4-e781-5f5f-92a7-681e75aeee0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124298/selection/d2ce58dcfde67b9e3e33c40dc0ec67c44464d31bf77f451e3f12f8c5805836bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-124298/selection/a67ba2ed67a73986443abb874c97f0c95a8b36be477f216946792b35dd801315" "q-124298/selection/d2ce58dcfde67b9e3e33c40dc0ec67c44464d31bf77f451e3f12f8c5805836bc" "q-124298/selection/b5742563c1be9789c9972480cc0398a9d68a3b4422fef1cb034bdb05841d249f" "q-124298/selection/f64772e64adfa06dcdc8b7e41d95f5a9112e5a1d7e5522bf9f6875c584882b1e" "q-124298/selection/98deb7f86f2e63ffd173e7b088d57fe256d622326f7ab344397f6876c121375f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124298" :question/id #uuid "9d9bcf07-4605-5aed-9b42-699d630fbd7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-124298" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/fd1956c8291f1bcecd7d37082110861ed7265fa40f7f85cbc69221cfdc5bea2d.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}(3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the ellipse $16{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=64,$ traversed from the point $(-2,0)$ to the point $(2,0),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\pi \\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =3(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =12{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =4{sin}^{2}⁡t+12({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =4{sin}^{2}⁡t+12 \\\\  & =4({sin}^{2}⁡t+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }4({sin}^{2}⁡t+3)\\cdot 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =16{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }({sin}^{2}⁡t+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124298/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0712bb6-c0f8-5551-8362-ae23629aa618"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124298"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124279/selection/21c2891af9757cd77cdd22461f3d2eb1543a48a48998a4afb96e73fea722aa2a" :answer/id #uuid "488b1f9e-3333-5037-a2bf-d0f0fb68feb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t){cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124279/selection/0ded6b9b1f978773fdba3f6c137c9975a6c6dab71a56252cd04c5b6d16c6b1e2" :answer/id #uuid "d1256954-7708-5d62-baf8-626e18df1d66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124279/selection/e7c200493d6d819f2ffddaaf9cd92943d3522ad4426d273b800c5f456637949f" :answer/id #uuid "c48d99a8-8c3d-5551-9788-85134800e3fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124279/selection/859e3bc74c6ff51be6112457d23ff16fc9c9394e2980e6c8fce1fffc2f26715f" :answer/id #uuid "e3246074-8f08-582e-86e7-acd116284e7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124279/selection/592f16270bdfd1eb600e886cd1d81f839c2d16e737a80707e8cfeb541c6ddff5" :answer/id #uuid "a822bae6-8045-5386-9ba2-1188953f51e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t){sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124279/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "855ea11f-f700-50ee-9ca1-faef0459d1fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124279/selection/0ded6b9b1f978773fdba3f6c137c9975a6c6dab71a56252cd04c5b6d16c6b1e2" :answer-field/choices ["q-124279/selection/21c2891af9757cd77cdd22461f3d2eb1543a48a48998a4afb96e73fea722aa2a" "q-124279/selection/0ded6b9b1f978773fdba3f6c137c9975a6c6dab71a56252cd04c5b6d16c6b1e2" "q-124279/selection/e7c200493d6d819f2ffddaaf9cd92943d3522ad4426d273b800c5f456637949f" "q-124279/selection/859e3bc74c6ff51be6112457d23ff16fc9c9394e2980e6c8fce1fffc2f26715f" "q-124279/selection/592f16270bdfd1eb600e886cd1d81f839c2d16e737a80707e8cfeb541c6ddff5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124279" :question/id #uuid "9a9948c5-d8d3-590c-a561-bf7eab258e30" :question/math-academy-id "q-124279" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/8d55ece1948f9ecb7da7d489b86a297651a34f409f83ba2470f6dd06678a375e.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}(x-y)\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along a circle of radius $3,$ traversed from the point $(0,-3)$ to the point $(0,3),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $3$ centered at $O.$ It can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x-y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124279/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0712bb6-c0f8-5551-8362-ae23629aa618"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124279"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124217/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "630178c2-09b8-58e4-a94b-964d54a30471" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124217/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "fbbd658f-57e1-58c6-8cfc-036d43369251" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124217/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "2f83ac87-faa5-50c7-abcb-a09f45135112" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124217/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "2aa3b20c-5895-5efe-9cd3-d66e4b766f29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124217/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "9b110a01-6001-563e-b05b-1a6e13b4cb16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124217/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc8c2968-b845-5ff0-870d-6527fbbee793" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124217/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-124217/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" "q-124217/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-124217/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-124217/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-124217/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124217" :question/id #uuid "3fa5ba0e-a6e5-5bfc-aa3b-ed7d15bd2173" :question/math-academy-id "q-124217" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/cb4c4828626255e26e298a0cdc202b37852df9d39bcfe15e0e67d350d90f774a.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}(\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi y}{2})+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path traversed along the line segment from the point $(2,0)$ to the point $(2,2),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(2,0)$ and $(2,2).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(2+t(2-2)),\\,(0+t(2-0))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,2t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi y}{2})+{x}^{2}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi (2t)}{2})+(2)^{2} \\\\  & =\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t+4)\\cdot 2\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4+\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2(4t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2[(4-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi )-(0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0)] \\\\  & =2[4-(-1)+1] \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124217/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b45822-868e-51bb-b551-345739e9ca44"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124217"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124173/selection/8a062f85dfae2453091ecd95389dc9b0751d8bb7c18126361428cf17100dc6b2" :answer/id #uuid "09c959ed-4813-579f-a3f9-64dce1b5e8e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124173/selection/6813ab1041b0710ec600e525b5dde1529e9cdde2099f23754ba54ec5d845bb88" :answer/id #uuid "a9ff833c-1efd-5aa4-9366-425b6f804796" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124173/selection/2bc5d83371a24844476947c013c304745bdc01e4bc7ab45335b74b409478e254" :answer/id #uuid "b517383b-4990-5d31-ab8b-9313eab1d73a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124173/selection/63079cc748dc757e7a8e5256fd2c9d955e6cf36193b2548b0f6e7b6b72fbf55c" :answer/id #uuid "daf188d1-566d-5f5a-b804-eabf124329de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124173/selection/e5c63bc832c49e18fb2678001d953240c26767b2f942793f012ef9f6442d3680" :answer/id #uuid "ae12dc20-00b4-5e1b-b9c3-1845eeb6cbf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124173/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "585fd08a-7633-5588-921d-98bd1d5da98b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124173/selection/6813ab1041b0710ec600e525b5dde1529e9cdde2099f23754ba54ec5d845bb88" :answer-field/choices ["q-124173/selection/8a062f85dfae2453091ecd95389dc9b0751d8bb7c18126361428cf17100dc6b2" "q-124173/selection/6813ab1041b0710ec600e525b5dde1529e9cdde2099f23754ba54ec5d845bb88" "q-124173/selection/2bc5d83371a24844476947c013c304745bdc01e4bc7ab45335b74b409478e254" "q-124173/selection/63079cc748dc757e7a8e5256fd2c9d955e6cf36193b2548b0f6e7b6b72fbf55c" "q-124173/selection/e5c63bc832c49e18fb2678001d953240c26767b2f942793f012ef9f6442d3680"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124173" :question/id #uuid "89e8c17a-70f5-584b-85ef-ba80154f3425" :question/math-academy-id "q-124173" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/dbd3fdd67ac209544717fc7d4b33831c7cdfd9f6839a7c1410f43ffd385d63ff.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}}{8y}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along the below-left quarter of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}=16,$ traversed from the point $(-4,0)$ to the point $(0,-1),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $4$ and $1,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\pi \\le t\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}}{8y}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+16(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}}{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{16{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{sin}^{2}⁡t}{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{16({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}(\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t})\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =-8{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-8t\\,{|}_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-8(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\pi ) \\\\  & =-8(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124173/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b45822-868e-51bb-b551-345739e9ca44"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124173"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124167/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "8dfadc7f-1009-5895-b38a-18492d81d6ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124167/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "5b317a52-c035-5a05-93a4-53442eba6780" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124167/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer/id #uuid "d90204f4-9ad8-5bff-b902-3b499909034b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124167/selection/f48b848c0ba9eb972a6ecdade8ce516585f3a0e3b5dbeab089775adb9307dc15" :answer/id #uuid "40de5b40-052a-5e88-9965-f847974bb880" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124167/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "276434ca-2fbd-523c-aa24-3dde9ac5a7a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124167/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e585aa64-fea0-5568-9283-e25d885d234c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124167/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer-field/choices ["q-124167/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" "q-124167/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" "q-124167/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" "q-124167/selection/f48b848c0ba9eb972a6ecdade8ce516585f3a0e3b5dbeab089775adb9307dc15" "q-124167/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124167" :question/id #uuid "9339ee88-5b7b-5154-84d1-4becde286df1" :question/math-academy-id "q-124167" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/559a6b6cb717c10e60b77da402e310fc5895c814655b4ca1748eba294d712a32.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{1}{2}xy\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the upper half of the circle of radius $2,$ traversed from the point $(2,0)$ to the point $(-2,0),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe curve $C$ is a half of a circle of radius $2$ centered at $O.$ It can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{2}xy,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ $\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =4{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{2}\\,(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{u}^{3}{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}[(1)^{3}-(-1)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-124167/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b45822-868e-51bb-b551-345739e9ca44"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124167"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124273/selection/596a129849400febbbd4509e3278c3c1cec667f8858cd6b38a14c1556b227002" :answer/id #uuid "77aab2e8-e5e1-5227-8b32-30c0c97e9205" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e}{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124273/selection/32e65fe743d0d028abb30010be473c4445ce2177c6c283fcc4d5963ada5dca86" :answer/id #uuid "1508d46d-4f62-5573-800c-20934d420471" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124273/selection/6e14fe454a5069957f908b06f75a89343262baa96a5485dcfc6bb403287c297d" :answer/id #uuid "44d7a797-e898-57b6-b9f3-a60aabc9c505" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(e-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124273/selection/5c80a8fc7c9404a6cac13c720b1b60ce1967ee57341778af99fbccd48bbae19e" :answer/id #uuid "8273cb1e-2976-5023-a521-d051a0994b0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}(e+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124273/selection/819734a35ad724a45c63e11a670acf5c03dbebb6acb50bd4dababee7c356c0d3" :answer/id #uuid "4d4b16ae-1d2f-5a52-89e4-3ce8ac8705fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}(e-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124273/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "daad3286-5dec-5714-bc03-63f59dfb5420" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124273/selection/819734a35ad724a45c63e11a670acf5c03dbebb6acb50bd4dababee7c356c0d3" :answer-field/choices ["q-124273/selection/596a129849400febbbd4509e3278c3c1cec667f8858cd6b38a14c1556b227002" "q-124273/selection/32e65fe743d0d028abb30010be473c4445ce2177c6c283fcc4d5963ada5dca86" "q-124273/selection/6e14fe454a5069957f908b06f75a89343262baa96a5485dcfc6bb403287c297d" "q-124273/selection/5c80a8fc7c9404a6cac13c720b1b60ce1967ee57341778af99fbccd48bbae19e" "q-124273/selection/819734a35ad724a45c63e11a670acf5c03dbebb6acb50bd4dababee7c356c0d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124273" :question/id #uuid "b8d0f290-7e22-532c-9147-08b82f839f9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-124273" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/0e5257867dae67451500793687a2da24ee31a73a17c691d8d8a6dcded46e8993.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}x{e}^{1-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along the three-quarters of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=9,$ traversed from the point $(0,1)$ to the point $(3,0),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $3$ and $1,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x{e}^{1-{y}^{2}}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t){e}^{1-{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{e}^{{cos}^{2}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{e}^{{cos}^{2}⁡t})\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =-9{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{e}^{{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u={cos}^{2}⁡t,$ $\\text{d}u=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{e}^{{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t & =-9{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{u}\\,(-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{e}^{u}{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}[{e}^{1}-{e}^{0}] \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot (e-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}(e-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-124273/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b45822-868e-51bb-b551-345739e9ca44"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124273"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124212/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "e8ef0de4-96dd-524e-b057-968697b1fad1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124212/selection/5d34995cddd0166b343cae457ee45643c04c739e08758db1204c66c5ee04158e" :answer/id #uuid "080ecbe0-5196-5ed7-9370-d5386ada71ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124212/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "14272cfc-5871-567c-8b91-a0533369d288" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124212/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "c9718596-27d4-51e6-9e51-37254aa84440" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124212/selection/4644593a6ae896793c595e8a37cd468ba91be6a8038e715c4c88cddad1968793" :answer/id #uuid "b036e90e-2ad3-592c-8f7f-76f03a814def" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124212/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c1fb21a-0b37-5f3d-905a-bab892d33ceb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124212/selection/4644593a6ae896793c595e8a37cd468ba91be6a8038e715c4c88cddad1968793" :answer-field/choices ["q-124212/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-124212/selection/5d34995cddd0166b343cae457ee45643c04c739e08758db1204c66c5ee04158e" "q-124212/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-124212/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-124212/selection/4644593a6ae896793c595e8a37cd468ba91be6a8038e715c4c88cddad1968793"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124212" :question/id #uuid "5f774621-da70-5079-af0a-f18fe6534c1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-124212" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/dfa95100566fce9ab113b00ae53d1a76e8977b68aa4bac0e9b6892a9930b70d4.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{y{x}^{2}+{y}^{3}}{8x}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the lower half of the circle of radius $4,$ traversed from the point $(-4,0)$ to the point $(4,0),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $4$ centered at $O.$ It can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\pi \\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{y{x}^{2}+{y}^{3}}{8x},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{3}}{8(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{64\\operatorname{sin}⁡t({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}{32\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\cdot (4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-8[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ] \\\\  & =-8(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124212/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b45822-868e-51bb-b551-345739e9ca44"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124212"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9512"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/4b5c788ad2c220b70a7f1d333680a70933f9b490a0db11fb3440dd3a2e06fa01.png)\n\nFind a definite integral that's equivalent to the line integral $\\displaystyle \\int_C (x+y) \\, \\textrm{d} x,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment from the point $(0,0)$ to the point $(3,3),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}x  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\dfrac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(0,0)$ and $(3,3).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨0+t(3-0),\\,0+t(3-0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3t,\\,3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0 \\le t \\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y) = x+y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =3t+3t \\\\  & =6t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6t\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =18{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9513"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/74033bfe17cefe62d5306b2186b9816ba26b816ece10c5dab5178abe1a9aaf89.png)\n\nFind the definite integral equivalent to the line integral $\\displaystyle\\int_C x^2 \\, \\textrm d y,$ where $C$ is the path along the ellipse $25x^2 + 4y^2 = 100,$ traversed from the point $(2,0)$ to the point $(0,5),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}y  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\dfrac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ can be parameterized as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\big\\langle 2\\cos{t}, \\: 5\\sin{t} \\big\\rangle, \\qquad 0 \\le t \\le \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y) = x^2,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}=4{cos}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(4{cos}^{2}⁡t)\\cdot 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =20{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{3}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9521"] :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_C \\left(x^2 + y^2\\right)\\,\\textrm d y,$ where $C$ is the path along the upper-right quarter of the circle $x^2 + y^2 = 4,$ traversed from the point $(2,0)$ to the point $(0,2),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058598/assets/8fc3a36829c9780c34e13f253d607c3849bfd3ef1399a77a79a3dd3d30ef7140.png)" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}y = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\dfrac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe curve $C$ is a quarter of a circle of radius $2$ centered at $O.$ It can be parameterized as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\big\\langle 2\\cos{t}, \\: 2\\sin{t} \\big\\rangle, \\qquad 0 \\le t \\le \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y) = x^2 + y^2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =4({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}4\\cdot (2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
